t/pulls/123789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123789","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123789.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123789.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-25T15:55:38Z"},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #123695\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\nWhen a directory is clicked in the filesystem dock, it's scanned for resources to import which is very expensive when there is a large number of them. I modified the logic in `FileSystemDock::_get_imported_files` which collects the resources, to skip directories containing a `.gdignore` file. It's only called once in `FileSystemDock::_update_import_dock()` before doing the expensive part which is loading each `.import` file twice for each collected file.\r\n\r\nThis changes behavior, but I'd argue now it's more in line with gdignore docs.\r\n\r\nI also noticed that the mechanism for updating the import dock can be very inefficient, so I'll try to to optimize it in the near future.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":